-- title:
--   Simple zero of p/(jₚ-jᵖ) at a supersingular value
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A` has characteristic $p$, is algebraically closed and has decidable equality, and let $\bar F$ be a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure. Let $C$ be a component chart for $A$, the field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` (the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$p$ modular function field) and $\bar F$: thus a valuation subring $C.\mathrm{integers}$ of that field together with a surjective residue map onto $\bar F$ with kernel the maximal ideal, a set of places, a finite set of nodes, a specialisation map on places, and the compatibility axioms of `ComponentChart`. Let $X \in \bar F$ and let $c \mapsto \mathrm{xpl}\,c$ assign to each $c \in k$ a place of $\bar F$ over $k$ such that for every $c$ and every polynomial $P$ over $k$ one has $\operatorname{ord}_{\mathrm{xpl}\,c} P(X) = \operatorname{mult}_c P$, the root multiplicity of $c$ in $P$. Assume the Laurent series $j$ (the $q$-expansion `jq`) and $j_p =$ `qExpand ℚ p jq`, viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, lie in $C.\mathrm{integers}$ with residues $X$ and $X^p$ respectively. Assume further $p \ge 5$ and let $a \in k$ satisfy $a \in$ `ssJSet p k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $p$, together with $a^{p^2} = a$, $a \neq 0$ and $a \neq 1728$. Then the element $p \cdot (j_p - j^{\,p})^{-1}$, with $p$ taken via the structure map from $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, lies in $C.\mathrm{integers}$, and its residue has order exactly $1$ at the place $\mathrm{xpl}\,a$.
--
--   The statement expresses, in chart-theoretic form, the classical fact coming from Kronecker's congruence for the modular equation $\Phi_p(j,j_p)$ that $p/(j_p - j^{\,p})$ is a uniformiser at each width-one supersingular point of the mod $p$ fibre of $X_0(p)$, where the two components meet. It is used by [`ModularCurve.isAttached_oppAnnulus_inftyChart_of_chartSpec`](thm.html#ModularCurve.isAttached_oppAnnulus_inftyChart_of_chartSpec) to verify that the opposite annulus is attached to the chart of the component through the cusp $\infty$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_natCast_mul_inv_nodeCoord_mem_integers_ord_residue_eq_one_inftyChart.lean

